{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Contrasting Benefits and Challenges of Cloud Computing "}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about benefits and challenges of cloud computing. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.   Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.  Exchanges simple information on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negociation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about disadvantages of cloud computing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify disadvantages applicable for me and my job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Design a brochure mentioning those disadvantages and some suggestions to solve them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your brochure with the class and discuss about it."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search for information about disadvantages of cloud computing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I identify disadvantages applicable for me and my job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design a brochure mentioning those disadvantages and some suggestions to solve them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share your brochure with the class and discuss about it."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Passive of modal verbs, have to"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "The <strong>passive voice</strong> with the modal verb <strong>have to</strong> refers to an obligation that goes upon the subject of the sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">When using the <strong>passive voice</strong> in English, represents a focus on the object of the sentence instead of the agent. By using the modal verb <strong>have to</strong> the sense of the sentence turns to an obligation or requirement. It means that something needs to be done compulsorily.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> The grammatical structure for using the <strong>passive voice</strong> with&nbsp;<strong>have to</strong>&nbsp;is:&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\">Subject + have/has &nbsp;+ To Be + Past participle + Complement&nbsp;</div><br /> <br /> For example:&nbsp;<br /> <br /> <i>Documents&nbsp;<strong>have to be checked</strong>&nbsp;in detail.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The cessation of services can cause no-payment matters, in other words, invoices have to be paid to avoid the service termination."}, {"type": "example", "content": "For instance, expert assistance has to be engaged by companies."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Electronic copies have to be given in order to get the information back, and also to obtain access to the software."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Besides, due diligence has to be implemented for companies to go over the vendor's performance and history. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs: Put up with, Back out of"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Inseparable phrasal verbs</strong> cannot have the object of the sentence in the middle of the phrasal verb, it must go after the preposition or adverb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>An <strong>inseparable phrasal verb</strong>, as its name says, cannot be separated. The verb plus the preposition have certain meaning by going together.&nbsp;<br /> <br /> For instance,&nbsp;<strong><i>put up with</i></strong>. It means to tolerate or to accept a situation.</p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>Customers don't have to&nbsp;<strong>put up with&nbsp;</strong>vendor's failures.</i></p> <p><strong><i>Back out of</i></strong> means to fail to keep a promise or an agreement.&nbsp;<br /> </p> <p>Example:</p> <p><i>Sometimes vendors&nbsp;<strong>back out of&nbsp;</strong>the contract and companies need to interfere.</i></p>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The operating characteristics have to be taking into account as well; so that the company backs out of what the vendor has promised"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If vendors back out of the agreement, customers don't need to put up with it in case they have more options."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If a customer loses access to his information, the company must maintain the back-up and recovery options."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pitfall"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an unexpected issue or problem"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Companies must contemplate the different benefits that computing and pitfalls offer."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "engage"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put influence over someone to perform an activity"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: For instance, expert assistance has to be engaged by companies. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "due diligence"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a term that involves investigation and research about something or someone in a company"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Besides, due diligence has to be implemented for companies to go over the vendor's performance and history."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hamstring"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to frustrate or restrict a process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is essential because services might hamstring the customer's tasks."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cessation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a termination or stopping of a process"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Customers must also know about the cessation of services that can cause no-payment matters."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob05aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can say aspects a customer needs to consider to make cloud services work."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about provisions to consider in case a cloud computing vendor fails in service. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss improvements and enhancements for cloud services. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some common concerns about cloud services?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are some agreements the vendor offers when getting cloud services?"}], "type": "